RESOURCE MANAGEMENT -- POLICY ON WEAPON SMUGGLING
Kazekage Office, disciplinary and treasury divisions

The desert caravans that sustain Sunagakure also tempt the smuggler. This policy
governs the illicit trade in weapons, poison, and puppet components.

Prohibitions:
1. No shinobi or contractor may divert village weapons, poison stock, or puppet
   parts to unauthorized buyers. Puppet and poison contraband is treated with
   special severity, given the danger of the forbidden arts falling into hostile
   hands (as the traitor Sasori's did).
2. Unregistered caravans crossing the Wind frontier are challenged and searched;
   smuggler movement is flagged to the border watch and reconnaissance cells.

Procedure:
- Recon and patrol report suspected smuggling to this office.
- Seized contraband is delivered to the Quartermaster or, for puppet/poison
  items, to the Puppet Brigade under seal.
- Verified smuggling by a shinobi is a grave offense, judged up to treason where
  it arms the village's enemies.

Vigilance on the caravan routes is every shinobi's duty. Sealed to the office.
